<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-COMBINED SLALOM FIRST LEG TIMES.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-COMBINED SLALOM FIRST LEG TIMES.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>First leg times from the</p>
<p>women's combined slalom at the Alpine skiing world championships</p>
<p>on Thursday (53 gates, vertical drop 140 metres):</p>
<p>1. Morena Gallizio (Italy) 44.13 seconds</p>
<p>2. Marlies Oester (Switzerland) 44.47</p>
<p>3. Hilde Gerg (Germany) 45.31</p>
<p>4. Sibylle Brauner (Germany) 45.73</p>
<p>5. Katja Seizinger (Germany) 45.86</p>
<p>6. Catherine Borghi (Switzerland) 45.87</p>
<p>7. Renate Goetschl (Austria) 46.21</p>
<p>8. Anita Wachter (Austria) 46.63</p>
<p>9. Miriam Vogt (Germany) 46.68</p>
<p>10. Marianne Kjoerstad (Norway) 46.89</p>
<p>11. Florence Masnada (France) 46.99</p>
<p>12. Iveta Kohutova (Slovakia) 47.83</p>
<p>13. Michaela Dorfmeister (Austria) 47.87</p>
<p>14. Marie Joelle Clement (Canada) 49.75</p>
<p>15. Maria Kvopkova (Slovakia) 49.84</p>
<p>16. Petra Bartlova (Czech Republic) 50.37</p>
<p>17. Carola Calello (Argentina) 50.85</p>
<p>18. Karolina Sedova (Czech Republic) 50.87</p>
<p>19. Anna Larionova (Russia) 53.37</p>
<p>20. Simona Pastinaru (Romania) 55.76</p>
<p>21. Svetlana Novikova (Russia) 57.44</p>
<p>Did not finish first run:</p>
<p>Pernilla Wiberg (Sweden)</p>
<p>Ingeborg Helen Marken (Norway)</p>
</text>
